   "RaceName": "State Representative Pos. 2",
   "Statement": "<b>Elected Experience</b><br/><br/><span>Gig Harbor Planning Commission.&nbsp;Endorsed by State Representative Michelle Caldier-Valdez, former State Representative Spencer Hutchins, and Key Peninsula Fire Fighters.</span><br/><br/><b>Other Professional Experience</b><br/><br/><span>Nonprofit leader, small business owner, and pastor with 18+ years leading teams, managing budgets, and developing successful programs that serve communities, families, refugees and empowering people out of poverty and addiction.</span><br/><br/><b>Education</b><br/><br/><span>Raised locally. South Kitsap High School graduate; Associate degree, Olympic College; Bachelor&rsquo;s in Psychology, NU; Masters in Nonprofit Leadership, Seattle U.</span><br/><br/><b>Community Service</b><br/><br/><span>Co-President, Walk In The Light International; VP, Heart for the City; Organized Christmas presents, food, school supplies, baby products drives alongside my husband and three children.</span><br/><br/><b>Statement</b><br/><br/><span></span>\r\n<p>You deserve a Washington where hard work still leads to opportunity, families can afford a home, small businesses can thrive creating good-paying jobs, and communities are safe. I&rsquo;m running because too many feel these opportunities are gone.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">I&rsquo;ve spent my life serving others, building solutions, and bringing people together to solve difficult problems with compassion and accountability.&nbsp;&nbsp;We can fix the root causes of our affordability crisis, strengthen public safety, support roads, bridges, and ferries, and<em> ensure the</em> <em>government serves people effectively through smarter spending, not higher taxes</em>.&nbsp;Let&rsquo;s fix what&rsquo;s broken in Olympia and restore opportunity for everyone.</span></p><br/><br/>",
