   "RaceName": "State Representative Pos. 2",
   "Statement": "<b>Elected Experience</b><br/><br/><span>First-time candidate for State Representative. Elected Faculty Representative, Tacoma Community College AFT-WA local.</span><br/><br/><b>Other Professional Experience</b><br/><br/><span>Special Educator, Holly Ridge Center. Adjunct Instructor, Tacoma Community College. Former CPS Investigator, Suquamish Tribe. Managed ECEAP, Early Head Start and childcare programs. Former small business owner.</span><br/><br/><b>Education</b><br/><br/><span>MS, Psychology, University of Phoenix. BA, History, Occidental College. Early Childhood Program Administration certificates, Olympic College.</span><br/><br/><b>Community Service</b><br/><br/><span>Representative, Salish Behavioral Health Administrative Services Organization Advisory Board. President, South Kitsap School District Native Education Parent Council. Home Visiting Advisory Member, Suquamish Early Learning Center. Former Tri-chair, DCYF Childcare Provider Supports Advisory Subcommittee.</span><br/><br/><b>Statement</b><br/><br/><p>Peninsula families are exhausted by housing costs, gridlock, unreliable ferries, and schools forced to do more with less. As an educator, working mom, and union member, I&rsquo;ve spent every day bettering the lives of our children and their families. I'll fight for home prices that match local wages, excellent public schools, and roads and ferries we&rsquo;ve waited decades for.</p>\r\n<p><em>Endorsed and Approved: 26th District Democrats, Kitsap Democrats, State Labor Council, Washington Education Association, American Federation of Teachers, National Women&rsquo;s Political Caucus, Washington Conservation Action, Planned Parenthood Alliance Advocates, Congressmember Emily Randall, County Councilmembers Hitchen and Denson, Commissioner Rolfes, and more.&nbsp;</em></p><br/><br/>",
